WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:15.405
"Whoa!" Zann cried as he and Darb ran.

2
00:00:15.425 --> 00:00:16.926
"What are those things?"

3
00:00:16.946 --> 00:00:18.266
"I don't know."

4
00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:22.068
Darb flapped his hands, trying to ward off the angry little creatures.

5
00:00:22.768 --> 00:00:26.590
They kept diving at the boys, stinging any exposed skin they could reach.

6
00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.331
"Let's go to the Hollow!

7
00:00:28.751 --> 00:00:31.072
It's close, and they probably won't follow us there."

8
00:00:31.888 --> 00:00:33.709
Zann glanced in the direction of the Hollow.

9
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:35.089
The place made him nervous.

10
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.651
It was a vacuum and magic didn't work in a vacuum.

11
00:00:39.631 --> 00:00:42.372
Most magical creatures feared and avoided such places.

12
00:00:43.113 --> 00:00:46.954
In fact, it was probably the only place Zann would never dare to go.

13
00:00:47.675 --> 00:00:50.316
In the Hollow he'd have no way at all to protect himself.

14
00:00:50.336 --> 00:00:53.197
"I've got a better idea," Zann said.

15
00:00:53.877 --> 00:00:56.698
He grabbed Darb's arm and then zapped them both away.

16
00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:00.660
They landed in another part of the swamp, far from the tiny dragons.

17
00:01:01.344 --> 00:01:02.985
"Whew!" Darb grimaced.

18
00:01:03.005 --> 00:01:05.025
"Can you do anything about these stings?"

19
00:01:05.045 --> 00:01:06.946
"Hold still."

20
00:01:07.326 --> 00:01:11.267
Zann rubbed his hands together and touched the red marks on Darb's arms and face.

21
00:01:11.987 --> 00:01:13.087
The marks faded away.

22
00:01:13.107 --> 00:01:15.048
"Thanks," Darb said.

23
00:01:15.748 --> 00:01:17.188
Zann healed his own stings.

24
00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:19.529
"So you don't know what those were?"

25
00:01:19.929 --> 00:01:20.369
he asked.

26
00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.950
"I thought you were an expert in that stuff."

27
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:24.831
Darb shook his head.

28
00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:30.500
"They looked like dragons, but the only dragons that small are mini flowersippers.

29
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:31.400
And you know what they're like.

30
00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.461
They don't sting."

31
00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:34.781
"Maybe they're not from Magica!"

32
00:01:35.141 --> 00:01:35.641
Zann said.

33
00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:38.162
"Maybe there's a wormhole near here."

34
00:01:38.182 --> 00:01:40.683
"You mean a portal to another world?"

35
00:01:40.963 --> 00:01:41.983
Darb looked doubtful.

36
00:01:42.003 --> 00:01:44.164
"I thought those were really rare.

37
00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:45.664
And really dangerous."

38
00:01:45.684 --> 00:01:47.265
"They are.

39
00:01:47.705 --> 00:01:50.166
Most people think my parents got lost in one.

40
00:01:51.046 --> 00:01:54.267
Or maybe went through an unstable one that closed behind them."

41
00:01:54.687 --> 00:01:56.047
Zann started to feel excited.

42
00:01:56.067 --> 00:01:59.356
"Let's go back and—oh!"

43
00:01:59.376 --> 00:02:00.897
Zann was nearly knocked off his feet.

44
00:02:01.238 --> 00:02:02.899
He grabbed a tree to steady himself.

45
00:02:02.919 --> 00:02:04.060
"What's wrong?"

46
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:04.881
Darb asked.

47
00:02:05.722 --> 00:02:07.083
The feeling had already passed.

48
00:02:07.103 --> 00:02:09.004
"It's Boz," Zann said.

49
00:02:09.024 --> 00:02:10.626
"I just felt him.

50
00:02:10.986 --> 00:02:11.927
He's not happy."

51
00:02:11.947 --> 00:02:13.568
"Was it a Red Share?"

52
00:02:14.629 --> 00:02:15.330
Zann nodded.

53
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.513
A Red Share happened when a Red felt an especially strong emotion.

54
00:02:20.214 --> 00:02:22.816
Any Red with a connection to the other Red would feel it too.

55
00:02:22.836 --> 00:02:27.420
"Boz probably just realized I sneaked out," Zann said.

56
00:02:28.092 --> 00:02:32.234
"It was a strong Share, which means he must be really mad.

57
00:02:33.114 --> 00:02:36.756
Or really scared—he seemed pretty worried about that warning.

58
00:02:37.256 --> 00:02:38.837
Either way I'd better get home."

59
00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:43.139
"Okay." Darb tucked an escaping panic bug back into his pocket.

60
00:02:43.159 --> 00:02:44.420
"See you tomorrow."

61
00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.922
"Yeah. If Boz doesn't lock me in the house with a Super Shield spell, that is."

62
00:02:50.682 --> 00:02:51.963
Zann rubbed his hands together.

63
00:02:51.983 --> 00:02:54.064
"Focus," he thought.

64
00:02:54.752 --> 00:02:58.574
The last thing he needed was to miss his mark and land on the roof or in Zing's

65
00:02:58.614 --> 00:02:59.174
food dish.

66
00:03:00.034 --> 00:03:03.216
Zap! He landed in the house's main room.

67
00:03:03.236 --> 00:03:04.956
"Right on target!"

68
00:03:05.316 --> 00:03:05.797
he murmured.

69
00:03:06.797 --> 00:03:09.478
He glanced around, but Boz was nowhere in sight.

70
00:03:10.078 --> 00:03:13.640
Instead Zann saw a man looking at the family pictures on the wall.

71
00:03:17.661 --> 00:03:18.022
are you?"

72
00:03:18.462 --> 00:03:19.262
Zann blurted out.

73
00:03:19.282 --> 00:03:21.523
"Where's my grandfather?"

74
00:03:22.223 --> 00:03:23.384
The stranger spun around.

75
00:03:24.236 --> 00:03:27.277
He was tall and gaunt, with glittering amber eyes.

76
00:03:28.117 --> 00:03:31.018
An odd expression flickered across his narrow face.

77
00:03:31.038 --> 00:03:33.759
"Another Red," the man said.

78
00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:35.999
He pointed at one of the blink images.

79
00:03:36.019 --> 00:03:38.920
"Are these your parents, young man?"

80
00:03:40.981 --> 00:03:43.942
Zann noticed his grandfather's diary on the floor under the table.

81
00:03:44.522 --> 00:03:45.362
That was strange.

82
00:03:45.682 --> 00:03:47.763
Boz never went anywhere without his diary.

83
00:03:48.423 --> 00:03:50.363
And he'd never leave it lying around on the floor.

84
00:03:50.383 --> 00:03:54.969
"That's none of your business," Zann told the stranger, suddenly nervous.

85
00:03:54.989 --> 00:03:56.449
"Where's Boz?"

86
00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:00.010
"Is that any way to speak to a guest in your home?"

87
00:04:00.810 --> 00:04:04.251
The corners of the man's thin lips twisted into a half smile.

88
00:04:04.271 --> 00:04:07.892
"I happen to be an old friend of your grandfather's."

89
00:04:08.732 --> 00:04:10.373
Zann wasn't sure what to say.

90
00:04:10.393 --> 00:04:12.233
"Boz?" he yelled.

91
00:04:12.253 --> 00:04:13.494
"Where are you?"

92
00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:15.274
The stranger smirked.

93
00:04:15.294 --> 00:04:18.355
"You can call as loudly as you like; he won't hear you.

94
00:04:18.975 --> 00:04:21.236
But I can take you to him if you wish."

95
00:04:22.392 --> 00:04:23.013
"Who are you?

96
00:04:23.473 --> 00:04:24.514
What are you doing here?"

97
00:04:24.894 --> 00:04:26.795
Zann clenched his fists at his sides.

98
00:04:26.815 --> 00:04:29.197
"And what have you done with Boz?"

99
00:04:30.238 --> 00:04:32.319
Just then he heard scratching at the door.

100
00:04:32.799 --> 00:04:36.442
Zing! Zann quickly rubbed his hands together and pointed at the door.

101
00:04:36.462 --> 00:04:38.624
"Open!" It flew open.

102
00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:42.947
Zing leaped into the room, shooting a stream of flame toward the stranger.

103
00:04:42.967 --> 00:04:44.708
"Good boy!"

104
00:04:45.148 --> 00:04:45.708
Zann cried.

105
00:04:45.728 --> 00:04:50.472
"That'll teach him to—" But quick as a wink, the stranger lifted his hand.

106
00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.581
“No!” shouted Zann.

107
00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:56.204
"Freeze!" said the stranger, pointing at the dragon.

108
00:04:56.925 --> 00:04:59.767
Zing instantly crashed to the floor, not moving.

109
00:04:59.787 --> 00:05:02.569
"Zing!" Zann fell to his knees.

110
00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.051
Zing was breathing very slowly.

111
00:05:05.712 --> 00:05:08.754
Realizing what the man had done, Zann turned to face him.

112
00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:11.857
"You used a Flash Freeze on him!"

113
00:05:12.237 --> 00:05:12.817
he accused.

114
00:05:12.837 --> 00:05:14.419
"That's illegal!

115
00:05:14.779 --> 00:05:16.020
He's a tame dragon!"

116
00:05:16.796 --> 00:05:22.678
Magica had few laws, aside from the important one taught to everyone from birth: Do no harm to

117
00:05:22.778 --> 00:05:29.359
others. But everyone knew that a Flash Freeze should only be used in emergencies such as immobilizing a

118
00:05:29.399 --> 00:05:31.480
large, rampaging wild dragon.

119
00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:34.821
It was never supposed to be used on people or pets.

120
00:05:34.841 --> 00:05:42.063
"I never did like dragons," the man said, examining the sparks that still ran across his hand.

121
00:05:42.083 --> 00:05:44.263
"Or Reds, for that matter."

122
00:05:44.964 --> 00:05:46.204
He rubbed his fingers together.

123
00:05:46.948 --> 00:05:52.651
Sparks leapt from his hand now, much more strongly than Zann would have expected from such a small

124
00:05:52.691 --> 00:05:53.471
amount of friction.

125
00:05:53.491 --> 00:05:57.373
"Freeze!" the man said, pointing toward Zann.

126
00:05:58.113 --> 00:06:02.155
Acting on instinct, Zann quickly grabbed Zing and rubbed his hands together.

127
00:06:02.916 --> 00:06:07.998
He felt the Flash Freeze sizzle within a hairbreadth of his face as he zapped himself and Zing

128
00:06:08.058 --> 00:06:11.860
away. Within half a second, they landed in the front yard.

129
00:06:12.576 --> 00:06:17.788
And half a second after that, Zann's house exploded into a million pieces.
